window.BIZ_PAPERS = (window.BIZ_PAPERS || []).concat([{"id": "HSC1-SAM", "unit": 1, "key": "SAM", "series": "Sample assessment (AAQ)", "date": "Pearson sample assessment material", "title": "Pearson sample paper", "source": "pearson", "kind": "exam", "code": "Sample", "spec": "new", "total": 80, "minutes": 90, "items": [{"q": 1, "sub": "a", "marks": 1, "section": "A", "ctx": ["Hura is a 60-year-old working in a manual job in a factory that makes bricks using heavy equipment that Hura has to carry around the factory. The work also requires welding, often in a cramped area, leading to Hura twisting the upper body and lifting heavy gas bottles, which has resulted in shoulder pain. To provide relief they have been taking painkillers and have now visited the General Practitioner who suggests that a programme of exercise may help."], "text": "Identify which healthcare professional can help Hura with appropriate exercises.\nA  Surgeon\nB  Radiographer\nC  Physiotherapist\nD  Podiatrist", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for the following:\n• C", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "b", "marks": 3, "section": "A", "ctx": [], "text": "State three ways that their shoulder pain may impact their overall health and\nwellbeing.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for each of the following up to a\nmaximum of three marks.\n• Poor quality of sleep\n• Reduction of social contacts\n• Reduced movement in shoulder\n• Low mood\n• Unable to concentrate\nAccept any other appropriate responses.\nDo not accept ‘pain’ on its own.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "c", "marks": 1, "section": "A", "ctx": ["Hura has regular health checks at work with a nurse. In the health check Hura says they feel stressed due to the targets to produce more bricks. The work environment is full of brick dust and Hura has not worn the masks supplied. Hura’s lung function is lower than normal."], "text": "State the branch of nursing concerned with assessing health in the workplace.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for the following:\n• Occupational Health", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "d", "marks": 2, "section": "A", "ctx": [], "text": "Explain one way that Hura may have a lower life expectancy than someone in an\noffice job.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for identification of an impact and one\nmark for an appropriate linked expansion, up to a\nmaximum of two marks.\n• More occupationally related health risks (1) due to\nmanual work (1)\n• Dusty environment can cause COPD (1), which may\nresult in premature death (1)\n• Working longer hours (1) due to lower income (1)\nAccept any other appropriate responses.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "e", "marks": 1, "section": "A", "ctx": ["Hura’s family has a history of cardiovascular diseases. Hura woke up one morning and could not use their right arm, it was diagnosed as a stroke."], "text": "Give the term that means you have an increased chance of developing a disease\nbased on your genetic makeup.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for the following:\n• Genetic predisposition", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "f", "marks": 1, "section": "A", "ctx": [], "text": "Give one lifestyle factor that could contribute to cardiovascular disease.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for the following:\n• Smoking\n• Lack of exercise\n• Substance misuse\n• Diet\nAccept any other appropriate response.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "g", "marks": 2, "section": "A", "ctx": [], "text": "Explain one way Roper and Tierney’s model of activities of daily living could be\nused to determine Hura’s care needs.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for identification and one additional mark\nfor an appropriate expansion, up to a maximum of two\nmarks.\n• Complete a systematic assessment (1) by\nconsidering each activity of daily living individually\n• Assessing what Hura can do in day-to-day life (1)\nwhich will enable a holistic care plan to be\ndeveloped (1)\n• Involving Hura in assessment (1) to complete a\nreview of every aspect of their life (1)\nAccept any other appropriate responses.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "h", "marks": 4, "section": "A", "ctx": [], "text": "Explain two ways an occupational therapist and a care worker can work together\nto support Hura.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for each identification and one mark for\nan appropriate linked expansion of each way, up to a\nmaximum of four marks.\n• Provide holistic care (1) by sharing responsibility\nbetween professionals (1)\n• Meeting all Hura’s needs (1) by working on one\nintegrated care plan (1)\n• Providing a seamless service (1) by communicating\nwith each other (1)\n• Giving Hura personalised care (1) by providing\ncomplementary services (1)\nAccept any other appropriate responses.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 1, "sub": "i", "marks": 9, "section": "A", "ctx": [], "text": "Assess the impact of Hura’s physical health conditions on their holistic\ndevelopment.", "ms": {"body": "Learners might refer to some/all of the following in their\nresponses, but learners should be rewarded for other pertinent\ncontextualised answers:\n• Physical – further physical decline by not moving due to pain or\nfear of further strokes\n• Physical – improved fitness due to improved exercise\nregime/medication/physiotherapy\n• Intellectual–improved physical fitness and care for body due to\nincreased knowledge about how to look after self and how to\nlearn about the diseases and how to slow down/minimise their\nprogression\n• Emotional – fear of illness and own mortality, changed self-\nperception as ill/patient\n• Social – increased social support via support groups. Increased\nsocial network from taking up active recreational\nactivities/social isolation due to decreased mobility\nMark scheme (award up to 9 marks) refer to specific marking guidance earlier\nin this document for more detail.\nLevel\nDescriptor\n0\nNo rewardable material.\nϭ\nϭ\u0003–\u0003ϯ\u0003\n• ;\u0004KϰĂͿ\u0003\n• •\nϮ\nϰ\u0003–\u0003ϲ\u0003\n• •\n• ϯ\nϳ\u0003–\u0003ϵ\u0003\n• •\n• Section B", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "a", "marks": 1, "section": "B", "ctx": ["Jace is a 14-year-old male who has just moved to a new area."], "text": "Identify a hormone associated with changes in puberty.\nA  Insulin\nB  Cortisol\nC  Oestrogen\nD  Adrenaline", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for the following:\n• C", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "b", "marks": 1, "section": "B", "ctx": [], "text": "Give one example of a primary sexual characteristic in a male.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for any of the following:\n• Penis\n• Testes", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "c", "marks": 3, "section": "B", "ctx": [], "text": "State three physical changes in puberty for a male.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for each of the following up to a maximum\nof three marks.\n• Penis and testicles enlarge\n• Deepening of voice/voice breaks\n• Increased muscle mass\n• Skeletal growth/widening of shoulders\nAccept any other appropriate response.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "d", "marks": 4, "section": "B", "ctx": ["Jace has made friends with a group of older boys who are encouraging him to drink alcohol. Jace likes drinking alcohol because it increases his confidence and makes him feel like he fits in with the older boys."], "text": "Explain two ways that alcohol can affect Jace’s physical development.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for each identification of a way and one\nmark for an appropriate linked expansion of each way, up\nto a maximum of four marks.\n• Too much scarring of the liver (1) leading to\ndiseases such as cirrhosis of the liver (1)\n• Lack of co-ordination/slurred speech (1) as alcohol\ninterferes with the brain’s communication pathways\n• Accidents and injury to the body (1) due to risk-\ntaking behaviour (1)\n• Increased susceptibility to illness/disease (1) as the\nimmune system is weakened (1)", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "e", "marks": 1, "section": "B", "ctx": ["Jace has started going to a youth club and the youth worker has noticed that Jace and his friends have often drunk alcohol before going to the club. The youth worker has started to run drug education sessions and has been talking to Jace about his mental health and where to go for support."], "text": "Give one setting other than a youth club where a youth worker may work.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for any of the following:\n• Schools\n• Faith-based groups\n• Colleges\n• Street projects\nAccept any other appropriate response.\nDo not accept youth centres.\n22\nϮĨ\u0003\n• •\n• •\n• •\n• •\nDĂƌŬ\u0003\n\u0003 Ϭ\u0003\n• ϭ\nϭ\u0003–\u0003ϯ\u0003\n• ;\u0004KϰĂͿ\u0003\n• •\nϮ\nϰ\u0003–\u0003ϲ\u0003\n• •\n• ϯ\nϳ\u0003–\u0003ϵ\u0003\n• •\nǁĂǇ͘ \u0003;\u0004KϯͿ\u0003\n•", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "f", "marks": 9, "section": "B", "ctx": [], "text": "Evaluate the role of a youth worker when working with Jace to prevent his alcohol\nuse becoming unhealthy.", "ms": {"body": "Mark against the command word and the marks available; see the levels descriptors for extended answers.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "g", "marks": 1, "section": "B", "ctx": [], "text": "State a definition of self-concept.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for any of the following:\n• An individual’s belief about themselves\n• A combination of self-image and self-esteem\n• An individual’s knowledge about who they are\nϮŚ\u0003\n• •\n• •\n• •\n• •\ndocument for more detail.\u0003\nDĂƌŬ\u0003\n\u0003\u0003 Ϭ\u0003\n• ϭ\nϭ\u0003Ͳ\u0003ϯ\n• ;\u0004KϰĂͿ\u0003\n• Ϯ\nϰ\u0003Ͳ\u0003ϲ\n• •\nϯ\nϳ\u0003Ͳ\u0003ϵ\n• •\nǁĂǇ͘ \u0003;\u0004KϯͿ\u0003\n24\nSection C", "levels": null}}, {"q": 2, "sub": "h", "marks": 9, "section": "B", "ctx": [], "text": "Discuss how Jace’s development can be influenced by peer pressure.", "ms": {"body": "Mark against the command word and the marks available; see the levels descriptors for extended answers.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "a", "marks": 1, "section": "C", "ctx": ["Avery is an 8-month-old infant who was born prematurely."], "text": "Identify an example of fine motor skills in infancy.\nA  Holding a pencil correctly\nB  Making balls with play dough\nC  Undoing and doing up buttons or laces\nD  Picking items up with thumb and forefinger", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for the following:\n• D", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "b", "marks": 1, "section": "C", "ctx": [], "text": "State one lifestyle factor that can contribute to premature birth.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for any of the following:\n• Smoking\n• Drinking alcohol\n• Substance misuse\nAccept any other appropriate response.\nDo not accept ‘diet’.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "c", "marks": 4, "section": "C", "ctx": ["Avery has been given the relevant vaccinations for babies under one year old."], "text": "Explain two ways that vaccinations can protect the community.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for each identification and one mark for\nan appropriate linked expansion of each way, up to a\nmaximum of four marks.\n• Herd immunity (1) reduces the amount of infectious\npeople (1)\n• They are not infectious to other people (1) because\nthe vaccine has created antibodies in their system\n• Diseases can be got rid of (1) if enough people are\nvaccinated (1)\u0003\n• Diseases cannot spread quickly (1) if a high\npercentage of people are vaccinated (1)\nAccept any other appropriate responses.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "d", "marks": 4, "section": "C", "ctx": ["As well as having vaccinations, Avery is also examined by the Health Visitor."], "text": "Explain two ways a Health Visitor can support Avery and their parents.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for each identification of a way and one\nmark for an appropriate linked expansion of each way, up\nto a maximum of four marks.\n• Check the baby is meeting physical development\nmilestones (1) by measuring and weighing baby (1)\n• Providing information/advice/guidance (1) on\ncare/development/wellbeing of baby (1)\n• Identify any health needs as early as possible (1) by\ncarrying out holistic assessment of the baby's health\nand wellbeing (1)\n• Identify possible safeguarding issues (1) by visiting\nthe home/family (1)\n• Reduce health inequalities (1) by\nreferring/signposting to services/sources of support\nAccept any other appropriate responses.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "e", "marks": 1, "section": "C", "ctx": ["Avery has only just started to bond with their mother after being in a neonatal unit when first born."], "text": "Give an action that helps an infant develop a bond with care givers.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for any of the following:\n• Cuddling/holding\n• Responding to crying\n• Make your newborn feel physically safe\n• Look into your newborn's eyes\n• Talking/singing to them\n• Smiling at them\nAccept other appropriate responses. \u0003\n1\n3f i)\nAward one mark for identification of a way, one mark for\nan appropriate linked expansion and one mark for a further\nexpansion, up to a maximum of three marks\n• Bonding makes a baby feel safe and protected (1)\nbecause this gives a secure attachment for\nemotional development (1) allowing for better future\nrelationships (1)\n• Baby will become more confident with other people\n(1) developing better relationships (1) that provides\na baby with a secure place to explore the world from\n• Insecure attachment (1) due to failure to bond (1)\nleads to less secure intimate relationships in the\nfuture (1)\nAccept any other appropriate responses.\n3\n3f ii)\nAward one mark for identification of a way, one mark for\nan appropriate linked expansion and one mark for a further\nexpansion, up to a maximum of three marks\n• Insecure attachment (1) because the baby is in an\nincubator (1) so there is less opportunity for\ncuddling (1)\n• Baby unable to bond with mother (1) as they are\nseparated (1) affecting future emotional\ndevelopment (1)\n• Baby may develop attachment disorder (1) as baby\ndoes not feel secure (1) due to the different people\ncaring for them (1)\nAccept any other appropriate responses.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "f(i)", "marks": 3, "section": "C", "ctx": [], "text": "Explain one reason for the importance of bonding with primary care givers.", "ms": {"body": "Mark against the command word and the marks available; see the levels descriptors for extended answers.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "f(ii)", "marks": 3, "section": "C", "ctx": [], "text": "Explain one way that being in a neonatal unit could impact bonding with\nAvery’s mother.", "ms": {"body": "Mark against the command word and the marks available; see the levels descriptors for extended answers.", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "g", "marks": 1, "section": "C", "ctx": ["Newborn hearing screening showed that Avery had hearing loss."], "text": "Give one example of intellectual development in an infant.", "ms": {"body": "Award one mark for any of the following:\n• Learning about environment through interaction\n• Recognise (familiar) faces\n• Starting to talk/babbling\n• Communicating with other people\nAccept any other appropriate responses.\n27 ϯŚ\n• •\n• •\n• •\n• •\n• •\n• •\n• •\n• •\ndocument for more detail.\u0003\n\u0003\u0003 Ϭ\u0003\n• ϭ\nϭ\u0003–\u0003ϯ\u0003 •\n• •\nϮ\nϰ\u0003–\u0003ϲ\u0003 •\n• •\nϯ\nϳ\u0003–\u0003ϵ\u0003 •\n28\n• ;\u0004KϯͿ\u0003\n• 29\nJuly 2024\nFor information about Pearson Qualifications, including Pearson Edexcel\nand BTEC qualifications visit qualifications.pearson.com\nEdexcel and BTEC are registered trademarks of Pearson Education Limited\nPearson Education Limited. Registered in England and Wales No. 872828\nRegistered Office: 80 Strand, London WC2R 0RL.\nVAT Reg No GB 278 537121", "levels": null}}, {"q": 3, "sub": "h", "marks": 9, "section": "C", "ctx": [], "text": "Assess how permanent hearing loss could affect Avery’s future development.", "ms": {"body": "Mark against the command word and the marks available; see the levels descriptors for extended answers.", "levels": null}}], "badge": "Pearson · current spec", "badgeTone": "new", "notice": "Pearson’s sample assessment for the current AAQ specification: the closest match to the real exam. Figures, tables and information booklets are described in words."}]);
